# Committed format fingerprints are compared byte-for-byte by
# `npm run capture:formats`. With core.autocrlf on (the Windows default) a
# checkout rewrote them to CRLF while the script writes LF, so every line
# differed and the drift check reported a changed format forever on a store
# that had not moved. The script normalizes line endings too; this keeps the
# committed form consistent in the first place.
tests/drift/fingerprints/*.json text eol=lf
